      3,
      "Positional Access, Field Separation, and Token Destruction",
      "Details the technical mechanics of positional access field separation, formally defining fields, values, and record rows to demonstrate how isolating metadata into a single top-level array eliminates repetitive key bloat. Contrasts single-typed tables with discriminator-based multi-typed bundles like 105db to show why structured matrix layouts mathematically eradicate token-weight hallucinations in large language model context windows while maintaining constant-time O(1) field-map memory lookups. Explains how this vector format achieves sub-50MB resident memory bounds on constrained edge hardware, paving the way for relational multi-table orchestration.",
